SUMMARY:Deadline 10:00 GMT: n-Space Fellowship\, second cohort (Prediction)
 : 18-month research fellowship at Somerset House Studios\, London (GBP 10\
 ,000 fee plus shared GBP 30\,000 R&D fund)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 07 Dec 2026 at 10:00 GMT.\n\nn-Space at Somerset House S
 tudios is a space for experimental\, collaborative research across art\, t
 echnology and society\, aimed at outcomes that do not fit traditional inst
 itutional platforms. Its second fellowship cohort is convened around PREDI
 CTION.\n\nOrganisation: Somerset House Studios\, with UAL Creative Computi
 ng Institute\, Abandon Normal Devices\, Lancaster University and the Natio
 nal Arts Council Singapore\; supported by the Rothschild Foundation\nLocat
 ion: Somerset House Studios\, London\, UK. London-track fellows must be ba
 sed in London and use the n-Space workspace at least two days a week. A se
 parate track brings one Singapore citizen or permanent resident to London 
 for three months.\nAward: London track: GBP 10\,000 fee and access to a GB
 P 30\,000 shared R&D fund\, with 24/7 workspace. No travel\, relocation or
  accommodation support. Singapore track: GBP 5\,000 fee plus return flight
 s\, accommodation\, per diems and ground transport\, and the same shared f
 und. Up to GBP 200 towards an access support worker for the application. N
 o application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 18 months\, April 2027 to Septembe
 r 2028 (Singapore track: nine months\, with April to June 2027 in London)\
 n\nMore: https://www.somersethouse.org.uk/somerset-house-studios/residenci
 es-and-opportunities/n-space-fellowship-open-call-predicition?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.somersethouse.org.uk/somerset-house-studios/residencies-and
 -opportunities/n-space-fellowship-open-call-predicition?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Somerset House Studios\, London\, UK. London-track fellows must be
